                <pb facs="0328" n="316" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg316"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/12312: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Rumania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gunther</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-06-22T12:00:00+02:00">June 22,
                            1941—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 2:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>570. My 569, June 21 [<hi rendition="#italic">22</hi>], 9 a.m. General Antonescu
                    has proclaimed full mobilization of the Rumanian land, air and marine forces,
                    and has himself taken command of the combined German-Rumanian forces on the
                    Rumanian front.</p>
                <p>Mihai Antonescu, formerly Minister without Portfolio, and recently Minister of
                    National Propaganda, has been named Vice President of the Council of Ministers,
                    and is charged with the exercise of the functions of the Leader of the State
                    during General Antonescu’s absence.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gunther</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
